|> Exercise
    handle=_dimensional_f^-1_g_f_

    !! Let $f$ be an invertible function with inverse $f^{-1}$.
    !! What constraints does the composition
    !! $$
    !! f^{-1} \circ g \circ f
    !! $$
    !! impose on the signatures of $f$ and $g$?

    Let $f$ be an invertible function with inverse $f^{-1}$ (cf. Exercise >>_dimensional_inverse_rule_).
    !! What signatures does the composition
    What is the most general signature of $f$ and $g$ for which the composition
    $$
    f^{-1} \circ g \circ f
    $$
    !! impose on $f$ and $g$?
    makes sense?

    !! For which signatures of $f$ and $g$ does the composition
    !! $$
    !! f^{-1} \circ g \circ f
    !! $$
    !! make sense,
    !! where $f$ is an invertible function with inverse $f^{-1}$?

    |> Solution

        This pattern requires $f$ and $g$ of the form

        $$
        \begin{gathered}
        f : [\tA] \ra [\tB] \\
        \up{1.6}g : [\tB] \ra [\tB]
        \end{gathered}
        $$

        since outputs of $f$ become inputs
        of $g$ and outputs of $g$ become inputs
        of 
        !! $f^{-1} : [\B] \ra [\A]$.
        $f^{-1}$, where $f^{-1} : [\B] \ra [\A]$ if $f : [\A] \ra [\B]$.

